#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-CG0398 expect=violation domain=DS
#note "EPOCH is absent, so the study never used epochs. The EPOCH exists guard was REMOVED (plan Q4): an absent column is a constant one, which cannot discriminate, so dropping it from the key is exact - the check adapts to `one DISPOSITION EVENT record per subject` and correctly flags the duplicate. Before the removal this study got silence. Pinned at 2 findings on subject 01-701-1015 and explicitly NOT on 01-701-1023. This rule is record-level, so an over-firing degradation would report 3 and `expect=violation` alone would pass on it - the count and the two row anchors are what exclude that."
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-2
#expectViolationCount 2
#expectViolationAt row=1 USUBJID=01-701-1015
#expectViolationAt row=2 USUBJID=01-701-1015
dataset DS label="Disposition"
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN   type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID  type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col DSSEQ    type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col DSCAT    type=Char label="Category for Disposition Event"
col DSSCAT   type=Char label="Subcategory for Disposition Event"
---
CDISCPILOT01 | DS | 01-701-1015 | 1 | DISPOSITION EVENT | STUDY PARTICIPATION
CDISCPILOT01 | DS | 01-701-1015 | 2 | DISPOSITION EVENT | STUDY PARTICIPATION
CDISCPILOT01 | DS | 01-701-1023 | 3 | DISPOSITION EVENT | STUDY PARTICIPATION
---
